From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] virtual: index the TEB/TSD retarget bitmap by bit, not by
 byte

data_map is a bitmap with one bit per word, but the TSD retarget indexed it
by byte, so it marked and tested the wrong words.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-bootstrap.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index 06904d8..dbc8682 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -4525,7 +4525,12 @@ int ios_jit_patch_x18(char *text_rw, char *text_rx, size_t text_size,
             uint32_t i0, i1, i2;
             unsigned reg;
 
-            if (data_map && (data_map[i / 4] || data_map[(i + 4) / 4] || data_map[(i + 8) / 4]))
+            /* Playport: data_map is a bitmap (one bit per word, as in the x18
+             * pass below); indexing it by byte skipped real triplets and read
+             * past the allocation beyond the first eighth of .text. */
+            if (data_map && ((data_map[(i / 4) >> 3] >> ((i / 4) & 7) & 1) ||
+                             (data_map[(i / 4 + 1) >> 3] >> ((i / 4 + 1) & 7) & 1) ||
+                             (data_map[(i / 4 + 2) >> 3] >> ((i / 4 + 2) & 7) & 1)))
                 continue;
 
             i0 = *(uint32_t *)(text_rw + i);
